# Rust build artifacts — never committed. `Cargo.lock` is the one exception:
# this crate now ships real, embedded, cryptographic WASM in every release
# artifact, and "document a pin instead of tracking it" (see
# docs/secure_runtime_alpha_8121_8200_cargo_lock_policy_decision.md,
# superseded by docs/secure_runtime_p0_closure_cargo_lock_policy_supersession.md)
# already measurably drifted once. `Cargo.lock` is tracked in version control
# — see the supersession doc above; do not re-add it here.
/target/
/build/
*.wasm
*.rlib

# WASM generation output (Stage 451, docs/runtime_wasm_generation.md) — the fixed
# `wasm-bindgen --out-dir` destination a future, separate stage would write real
# generated `.wasm`/JS glue/`.d.ts` files into. Nothing is generated by this stage;
# this pattern exists so that IF a future stage ever runs `npm run build:wasm`
# (package.json, Stage 450), its output is never accidentally staged or committed.
/pkg/
